    "text": "To determine how much money Dawn makes per hour, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total time Dawn spends painting the 12 paintings.\n2. Determine Dawn's hourly wage by dividing her total earnings by the total time spent painting.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total time Dawn spends painting the 12 paintings. Since it takes her 2 hours to paint one painting, the time to paint 12 paintings is:\n\\[ 12 \\text{ paintings} \\times 2 \\text{ hours/painting} = 24 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNext, we know that Dawn earns $3,600.00 for these 12 paintings. To find out how much she makes per hour, we divide her total earnings by the total time spent painting:\n\\[ \\frac{3600 \\text{ dollars}}{24 \\text{ hours}} = 150 \\text{ dollars/hour} \\]\n\nTherefore, Dawn makes \\(\\boxed{150}\\) dollars per hour.",
